# no-deferral.waivers — the committed allowlist for `cargo xtask gate no-deferral`.
#
# FORMAT:  <MATCHER><TAB><reason> [owner: <role>] [retires: <TRACKER-ID>]
#   MATCHER is an EXACT `path:line`. A matcher without a trailing `:<digits>` is REFUSED at load —
#   see "ONE GLOB USED TO STAND HERE" below. A marker (file:line) is WAIVED when a row equals it.
#   Every row must end in `[retires: <ID>]` naming the row of docs/design/1.6.0-TRACKER.md that
#   retires it. A row with no such tag, or one naming a tracker row that does not exist, is RED.
# The allowlist is a FLOOR CHECKED BOTH WAYS: a marker not waived is RED (over-count); a waiver that
# matches no marker is RED (stale — the marker was resolved). See xtask/src/gates/no_deferral.rs
# and docs/design/playbook/gate-no-deferral.md.
#
# no-deferral-strict-done (what scripts/verify-1.6.0-done.sh runs) additionally FAILS if ANY row below is not a
# */hot/* row: the hot/* foundation fixtures are the ONE permanent exemption; the voice skeleton rows
# are TRACKED 1.6.0 debt that MUST be gone before 1.6.0 is done.
#
# ── WHY THIS FILE WAS REGENERATED, 2026-09-22 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The previous revision DID NOT DESCRIBE THIS TREE, and both halves of the gate said so at once:
#
#     52 waiver rows      39 pointed at a line holding NO marker        (`:stale-waiver` RED)
#     52 real markers     38 of them were waived by nothing at all      (`:unwaived`     RED)
#
# Not one of the 44 `host.rs` rows matched a marker: the rows named lines 855–1217, the markers were
# at 997–1359 — the first off by +142, the last by +142, with the drift NOT constant across the file
# (decl.rs had not moved at all). The record described that as "a mechanical +1 line-number resync of
# 44 rows … verified: 44 rows". It was not +1, it was not verified, and a "+1 resync" cannot be
# mechanical when one of the two files did not move. **A waiver file that describes a different tree
# excuses nothing and hides everything** — the 38 real markers it failed to name were, for as long as
# it stood, undeclared deferrals in shipped source with no reason and no owner.
#
# REGENERATE, NEVER HAND-PATCH. The line numbers below were not typed; they came out of the gate:
#
#     cp scripts/no-deferral.waivers /tmp/w.bak
#     grep '^#' scripts/no-deferral.waivers > scripts/no-deferral.waivers   # rows removed, header kept
#     cargo xtask gate no-deferral        # `:unwaived` now enumerates EVERY real marker, in order
#     cp /tmp/w.bak scripts/no-deferral.waivers                             # restore, then re-emit rows
#
# With zero rows loaded every marker is un-waived, so the gate's own `:unwaived` line IS the marker
# census. That is the only source a row's line number may come from. Reading them off the file by eye
# is what produced the revision this one replaces.
#
# ── ONE GLOB USED TO STAND HERE, AND IT WAIVED WHATEVER APPEARED ─────────────────────────────────
# The single row `crates/busbar-plugin/src/hot/*` covered all 52 markers, never expired, and matched
# every marker any future edit put anywhere under that tree. The stale-waiver check could not fire on
# it either: one glob matching 52 markers stays "used" until the last one goes, so 51 could be
# resolved and the row would still look live. It was, in effect, a permanent unreviewed exemption for
# a whole directory.
#
# So the markers are enumerated one per line, each naming the slot it exempts and the tracker row
# that retires it. This costs a line-number edit whenever these files move — which is the point: the
# gate's stale-waiver check then reports exactly which exemptions no longer describe the tree,
# instead of a glob absorbing the change in silence.
#
# ── WHAT THESE 52 ROWS ARE, STATED SO IT CANNOT BE MISREAD AS A SKIP ─────────────────────────────
# `mod stub` / `PlaneHostVtable::STUB` / `PlaneDecl::STUB` are a COMPILE-SURFACE PROOF, not a
# postponed capability. Each fn has the exact fn-pointer signature of its vtable slot, so the module
# type-checks that every `extern "C-unwind"` slot in the ABI has a real, well-typed signature; a STUB
# slot panics BY DESIGN because nothing is ever meant to dispatch through it. Measured: the only
# consumers of either constant in the whole tree are this crate's own tests —
#   crates/busbar-plugin/src/hot/tests/host_tests.rs:77,128,138,145,157,222
#   crates/busbar-plugin/src/hot/tests/decl_tests.rs:29
# A fixture whose callers are the tests that check its types is not a deferral, and these rows do not
# claim a future release will fix it. They are exempt because the thing they mark is FINISHED.
#
# ── THE THING THAT *IS* OPEN, AND IT IS 1.6.0 WORK: H6 ───────────────────────────────────────────
# The previous revision retired all 52 rows against H5, whose text read "Out of 1.6.0 scope; the work
# lands with docs/design/1.6.0-protocols-as-plugins.md" — a DECISIONS #15 banned phrase pointing at a
# file that has never existed in this repository (`git cat-file -e HEAD:docs/design/1.6.0-protocols-as-plugins.md`
# fails; the same non-existent file is cited four more times in 1.6.0-duplex-plane-and-realtime.md).
# 52 markers were waived, in banned words, against a document that is not there.
#
# **AND THAT IS THE WORSE HALF OF THE DEFECT, NOT THE LESSER ONE.** The 39 bad line-anchors were loud:
# the gate reported them by name every run. An unreachable EXIT CONDITION is silent. A waiver whose
# retirement test cannot be evaluated never retires — it is permanent by accident rather than by
# decision, and it looks identical to a healthy row while it happens. Every row below now retires
# against H5, whose condition is a COMMAND THAT RUNS AGAINST THIS TREE:
#
#     grep -rn "PlaneHostVtable::STUB\|PlaneDecl::STUB" crates/     # empty => H5 is done
#
# and H5 in turn names H6, whose condition is also a command:
#
#     grep -rln "PlaneHostVtable" crates/busbar-plane-*             # non-empty => H6 is done
#
# Neither names a document. A retirement condition that cannot be run is not a condition.
#
# That framing also hid a real 1.6.0 row. BUSBAR-1.6.0.md §11a makes *"`PlaneHost` (+ cost carrier) has
# REAL production riders (dogfooded, step 2) — no '0-caller ABI'"* a **CUT GATE** for 1.6.0, and the tree
# does not meet it. **State the gap precisely, because the obvious reading is wrong and this file made
# that mistake once already:** the HOST IS BUILT. `build_plane_host_vtable()`
# (crates/busbar-kernel/src/plane_host/vtable.rs:36) wires 44 of 44 slots to real implementations across
# 13,054 lines in crates/busbar-kernel/src/plane_host/ — including cost_reserve/cost_settle at
# vtable.rs:121-122 over cost_host.rs (224 lines). The 52 markers below are NOT that host and never were.
# What is missing is a RIDER: `grep -rln "PlaneHostVtable" crates/busbar-plane-* crates/busbar-{llm,mcp,a2a,voice}`
# returns ZERO — every installed plane rides the neutral Rust seam (EngineHost), not the C-ABI vtable.
# So the FIXTURES are finished (H5) and the DOGFOODING is owed (H6). Splitting them is what lets these
# rows be permanent without that permanence quietly covering an open cut gate.
#
# Rows tagged `HOT:` mark a slot a plane already exercises through the NEUTRAL seam — cost_reserve and
# cost_settle, ported at crates/busbar-voice/src/runtime/metering.rs:350,389. Their fixture is still just
# a fixture and the waiver stands unchanged; the tag exists so nobody reads "waived" as "unridden", which
# is exactly backwards for those two.
#
# ── busbar-voice: the SKELETON / "dev-only until DoD" markers are CLEARED ───────────────────────────
# The voice plane's IR + both dialect codecs + T2 runtime + both topologies are implemented (behind the
# "runtime" feature) and the plane is installed at boot behind `plane-voice`; the stale SKELETON /
# "dev-only until DoD" marker prose in busbar-voice src has been reworded to truthful current-state, so
# no waiver rows remain for it. (Any residual "dev-only until DoD" prose outside busbar-voice src — e.g.
# the config-schema tracking note or the composition-root feature comment — is its own row, not this one's.)

